    "summary": "# Key Changes in FCC/Key4hep Ecosystem (2026-09-15 to 2026-09-22)\n\n## Breaking / Potentially Impactful Changes\n\n- **AIDASoft/DD4hep#1681**: The CSG-based exporter has been removed from DDCAD; downstream workflows relying on it for CAD conversions will need to migrate to the remaining export paths.\n- **AIDASoft/DD4hep#1663**: `Geant4Output2EDM4hep` now retrieves the run object from the worker context, fixing multi-threaded simulation output but potentially altering behavior for custom output plugins built on the old API.\n- **key4hep/k4ActsTracking#98**: Adapts to updated ACTS APIs, which is required to keep tracking builds working against current ACTS but may affect anyone pinned to intermediate ACTS versions.\n- **key4hep/k4ActsTracking#87**: The ACTS TGeo plugin is no longer built in CI, signalling a move away from TGeo-based geometry conversion in favor of the blueprint/Gen3 approach.\n- **key4hep/k4ActsTracking#97**: `--compactFile` is now required for the CKF, GNN, and geometry-visualization entry points; existing user scripts that omitted it will fail loudly instead of silently misbehaving.\n\n## New Features\n\n- **key4hep/k4FWCore#431**: Adds an `--evt-max` alias to `k4run`, aligning the CLI with Gaudi/Athena conventions and easing script portability.\n- **key4hep/k4FWCore#427**: Refactors test components to functional algorithms, providing more up-to-date reference implementations for developers writing new Gaudi functional algorithms.\n- **key4hep/k4geo#662**: New utility that maps detector volumes to their closest predefined ROOT color, improving event-display and geometry-visualization consistency.\n- **key4hep/k4geo#658**: Updated MUSIC (muon collider) geometry with instrumented nozzles \u2014 relevant for background and detector-performance studies at a muon collider.\n- **key4hep/k4ActsTracking#104**: Adds support for named ACTS material-map fields, enabling more flexible material-map configurations in tracking reconstruction.\n- **hep-fcc/FCC-config#386**: Adds a track-validation option (and ctests) for IDEA, giving FCC-ee analyzers a standardized way to validate tracking outputs.\n- **hep-fcc/FCCeePhysicsStudies#61**: Adds FSR beam parameters, important for precision electroweak and Higgs studies at FCC-ee.\n- **hep-fcc/fcc-drs#88**: DIRAC/iLCDirac production IDs are now tracked on campaign-assigned requests, improving traceability of centrally produced datasets.\n\n## Important Bug Fixes\n\n- **key4hep/k4GaudiPandora#54**: Fixes PFO comparison against the current EDM4hep, restoring correct behavior of Pandora-based particle-flow reconstruction with recent EDM4hep releases.\n- **hep-fcc/k4RecCalorimeter#284**: Only looks for Boost when building tests, unblocking calorimeter-reconstruction builds in environments without a full Boost installation.\n- **AIDASoft/DD4hep#1666**: Updated FCC MDI synchrotron-radiation mask geometry, improving fidelity of machine-detector-interface backgrounds in FCC-ee simulations.",
